{"entries":{"tdata:src/index.ts":{"doclets":[],"fp":"95ac98ff4cd2c59a37e82a1464224b14993db02726ff6bee37c463fb228abd31","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","symbols":0,"lastUsed":1795601953045},"md:src/index.ts":{"fp":"d135ebda6615f6d4fd560b0806f7866014ac30c4c9128b3ba4e3533d6d0c504c","issues":[],"kind":"md","skipped":"no-jsdoc","symbols":0,"lastUsed":1795601953046},"tdata:src/environment.ts":{"doclets":[],"fp":"928a29da9b4ad9ba22b73894805d6392bbb227bd5101afd09c95bf40ad33c63c","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","symbols":0,"lastUsed":1795601953051},"md:src/environment.ts":{"fp":"a4eec690e26e163e8922d6f556bfa4ace814be9fb5ebe634e7290c677507d8db","issues":[],"kind":"md","skipped":"no-jsdoc","symbols":0,"lastUsed":1795601953053},"tdata:src/basic-auth.module.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"BasicAuthModule","longname":"BasicAuthModule","name":"BasicAuthModule","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"Minimal NestJS module for the Basic auth guard.\n\n`forRoot(options?)` returns a `DynamicModule` that provides `BasicAuthGuard`\nwith the resolved options (via `useFactory`, so the guard carries them\nregardless of how Nest instantiates it).","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":44},"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"dist/basic-auth.module.js:17","src":"src/basic-auth.module.ts:13"},"level":0},{"id":"BasicAuthModule.forRoot","longname":"BasicAuthModule.forRoot","name":"forRoot","kind":"function","scope":"static","description":"Registers `BasicAuthGuard` as a provider carrying `options`.","memberof":"BasicAuthModule","params":[{"description":"Guard options; omitted values fall back to the environment/defaults.","name":"options","type":{"names":["BasicAuthOptions"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"A `DynamicModule` exporting `BasicAuthGuard`.","type":{"names":["DynamicModule"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":63},"order":1,"mdaics":{"dist":"dist/basic-auth.module.js:23","src":"src/basic-auth.module.ts:19"},"level":0}],"fp":"4b2988422428a54c4a9f46bf5877c3d201dac31734df3ccad0188955ac1ca6c2","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","symbols":0,"lastUsed":1795601953099},"md:src/basic-auth.module.ts":{"fp":"215c405e6235d5c1dfdfceec1d4af2f7c6d030364821d135f4915ab1ad1caa14","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"<a name=\"BasicAuthModule\"></a>\n\n## BasicAuthModule\nMinimal NestJS module for the Basic auth guard.\n\n`forRoot(options?)` returns a `DynamicModule` that provides `BasicAuthGuard`\nwith the resolved options (via `useFactory`, so the guard carries them\nregardless of how Nest instantiates it).\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: src/basic-auth.module.ts:13  \ndist: dist/basic-auth.module.js:17\n<a name=\"BasicAuthModule.forRoot\"></a>\n\n### BasicAuthModule.forRoot(options) ⇒ <code>DynamicModule</code>\nRegisters `BasicAuthGuard` as a provider carrying `options`.\n\n**Kind**: static method of [<code>BasicAuthModule</code>](#BasicAuthModule)  \n**Returns**: <code>DynamicModule</code> - A `DynamicModule` exporting `BasicAuthGuard`.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| options | <code>BasicAuthOptions</code> | Guard options; omitted values fall back to the environment/defaults. |\n\nsrc: src/basic-auth.module.ts:19  \ndist: dist/basic-auth.module.js:23\n","symbols":2,"lastUsed":1795601953270},"tdata:src/basic-auth.guard.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"<anonymous>~BasicAuthGuard()","longname":"<anonymous>~BasicAuthGuard","name":"BasicAuthGuard","kind":"constructor","memberof":"<anonymous>~BasicAuthGuard","params":[{"description":"Guard options; omitted values fall back to the environment/defaults.\n  Invalid `credentials` entries throw at construction.","name":"options","type":{"names":["BasicAuthOptions"]}}],"order":6,"returns":[{"type":{"names":["BasicAuthGuard"]}}]},{"id":"BasicAuthGuard","longname":"BasicAuthGuard","name":"BasicAuthGuard","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"Guards a route with the HTTP Basic authentication scheme (RFC 7617), wrapping\nthe [`basic-auth`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/basic-auth) package (`parse`).\n\nCredentials are resolved in order (first source that yields credentials wins):\n\n1. the standard `Authorization` header via `parse()` — when the header is\n   present it is authoritative (an empty value falls through, a malformed one\n   rejects the request);\n2. the custom `headerNames` headers (`x-auth-username`/`x-auth-password` by\n   default) when both values are non-empty strings;\n3. the request body `auth.username`/`auth.password` when `body: true` is set.\n\nOn success: sets `req.user` to the validated credentials.\nOn failure: sets `WWW-Authenticate` on the response and throws `UnauthorizedException`.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":117},"order":4,"mdaics":{"dist":"dist/basic-auth.guard.js:89","src":"src/basic-auth.guard.ts:139"},"level":0},{"id":"readHeader","longname":"readHeader","name":"readHeader","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Read a header by name: Node normalizes names to lowercase, so try the name as\ngiven and fall back to its lowercase form. Non-string and non-string-array\nvalues count as absent.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":58},"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"dist/basic-auth.guard.js:30","src":"src/basic-auth.guard.ts:78"},"returns":[{"type":{"names":["string"]}}],"level":0},{"id":"customHeaderCredentials","longname":"customHeaderCredentials","name":"customHeaderCredentials","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Credentials from the custom headers: returned only when both `username` and\n`password` are non-empty strings (absent/non-string/empty means \"not provided\").","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":69},"order":1,"mdaics":{"dist":"dist/basic-auth.guard.js:41","src":"src/basic-auth.guard.ts:89"},"returns":[{"type":{"names":["Credentials"]}}],"level":0},{"id":"bodyCredentials","longname":"bodyCredentials","name":"bodyCredentials","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Credentials from a parsed request body: `body.auth.username` / `body.auth.password`,\nread with own-property checks only (a crafted body with inherited `auth` is not trusted).","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":78},"order":2,"mdaics":{"dist":"dist/basic-auth.guard.js:50","src":"src/basic-auth.guard.ts:99"},"returns":[{"type":{"names":["Credentials"]}}],"level":0},{"id":"timingSafeCompare","longname":"timingSafeCompare","name":"timingSafeCompare","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Compare two strings in constant time. Both buffers are padded to the same\nlength so `timingSafeEqual` runs unconditionally — it neither throws nor\nshort-circuits, so timing reveals neither the lengths nor the value.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":95},"order":3,"mdaics":{"dist":"dist/basic-auth.guard.js:67","src":"src/basic-auth.guard.ts:115"},"returns":[{"type":{"names":["boolean"]}}],"level":0},{"id":"BasicAuthGuard#expectedPairs","longname":"BasicAuthGuard#expectedPairs","name":"expectedPairs","kind":"member","scope":"instance","description":"Expected credentials as buffers, cached on first use (options/environment are fixed after construction).","memberof":"BasicAuthGuard","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":210},"order":12,"mdaics":{"dist":"dist/basic-auth.guard.js:169","src":"src/basic-auth.guard.ts:224"},"returns":[{"type":{"names":["{ name: Buffer; pass: Buffer; }[]"]}}],"level":0},{"id":"BasicAuthGuard#canActivate","longname":"BasicAuthGuard#canActivate","name":"canActivate","kind":"function","scope":"instance","description":"NestJS guard entry point: resolves and validates credentials from the request.","memberof":"BasicAuthGuard","params":[{"description":"The NestJS execution context (HTTP request/response).","name":"context","type":{"names":["ExecutionContext"]}}],"returns":[{"description":"`true` when authenticated; throws `UnauthorizedException` (401) with a\n  `WWW-Authenticate` challenge otherwise.","type":{"names":["boolean"]}}],"meta":{"lineno":149},"order":7,"mdaics":{"dist":"dist/basic-auth.guard.js:108","src":"src/basic-auth.guard.ts:157"},"level":0},{"id":"BasicAuthGuard#resolveCredentials","longname":"BasicAuthGuard#resolveCredentials","name":"resolveCredentials","kind":"function","scope":"instance","description":"Resolve credentials in order:\n\n1. the standard `Authorization` header — when present it is authoritative\n   (a present-but-unparseable value rejects the request, no fallback);\n2. the custom `headerNames` headers, when both values are non-empty strings;\n3. the request body pair, when `body: true` is set.","memberof":"BasicAuthGuard","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":167},"order":8,"mdaics":{"dist":"dist/basic-auth.guard.js:126","src":"src/basic-auth.guard.ts:176"},"returns":[{"type":{"names":["Credentials"]}}],"level":0},{"id":"BasicAuthGuard#fallbackSources","longname":"BasicAuthGuard#fallbackSources","name":"fallbackSources","kind":"function","scope":"instance","description":"Fallback credential sources, consulted in order after the standard header.","memberof":"BasicAuthGuard","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":179},"order":9,"mdaics":{"dist":"dist/basic-auth.guard.js:138","src":"src/basic-auth.guard.ts:188"},"returns":[{"type":{"names":["CredentialSource[]"]}}],"level":0},{"id":"BasicAuthGuard#reject","longname":"BasicAuthGuard#reject","name":"reject","kind":"function","scope":"instance","description":"Sets the `WWW-Authenticate: Basic realm=\"...\"` challenge (realm escaped per RFC 7617) and throws a 401.","memberof":"BasicAuthGuard","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":186},"order":10,"mdaics":{"dist":"dist/basic-auth.guard.js:145","src":"src/basic-auth.guard.ts:196"},"returns":[{"type":{"names":["never"]}}],"level":0},{"id":"BasicAuthGuard#challenge","longname":"BasicAuthGuard#challenge","name":"challenge","kind":"function","scope":"instance","description":"The `WWW-Authenticate` challenge string with the realm escaped per RFC 7617.","memberof":"BasicAuthGuard","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":197},"order":11,"mdaics":{"dist":"dist/basic-auth.guard.js:156","src":"src/basic-auth.guard.ts:207"},"returns":[{"type":{"names":["string"]}}],"level":0},{"id":"BasicAuthGuard#isValidCredentials","longname":"BasicAuthGuard#isValidCredentials","name":"isValidCredentials","kind":"function","scope":"instance","description":"Constant-time check of the provided credentials against every expected pair.\nBoth comparisons always run and are length-padded, so a mismatch in username\ndoes not skip the password check (no timing oracle on the username or on the\nexpected password length).","memberof":"BasicAuthGuard","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":229},"order":13,"mdaics":{"dist":"dist/basic-auth.guard.js:188","src":"src/basic-auth.guard.ts:246"},"returns":[{"type":{"names":["boolean"]}}],"level":0},{"id":"<anonymous>~BasicAuthGuard","longname":"<anonymous>~BasicAuthGuard","name":"BasicAuthGuard","kind":"class","scope":"inner","memberof":"<anonymous>","meta":{"lineno":137},"order":5,"mdaics":{"dist":"dist/basic-auth.guard.js:90","src":"src/basic-auth.guard.ts:146"}}],"fp":"e9373102c7405d763e05901a14c078b7b9d11be41c3dfda75effde17839b5710","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","symbols":0,"lastUsed":1795601953302},"md:src/basic-auth.guard.ts":{"fp":"a4cbabbb9d2432c909f3c723d98c4fc534a826e17a2ce99ccfb08381e618e062","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Members\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#BasicAuthGuard\">BasicAuthGuard</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Guards a route with the HTTP Basic authentication scheme (RFC 7617), wrapping\nthe <a href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/basic-auth\"><code>basic-auth</code></a> package (<code>parse</code>).</p>\n<p>Credentials are resolved in order (first source that yields credentials wins):</p>\n<ol>\n<li>the standard <code>Authorization</code> header via <code>parse()</code> — when the header is\npresent it is authoritative (an empty value falls through, a malformed one\nrejects the request);</li>\n<li>the custom <code>headerNames</code> headers (<code>x-auth-username</code>/<code>x-auth-password</code> by\ndefault) when both values are non-empty strings;</li>\n<li>the request body <code>auth.username</code>/<code>auth.password</code> when <code>body: true</code> is set.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>On success: sets <code>req.user</code> to the validated credentials.\nOn failure: sets <code>WWW-Authenticate</code> on the response and throws <code>UnauthorizedException</code>.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#readHeader\">readHeader()</a> ⇒ <code>string</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Read a header by name: Node normalizes names to lowercase, so try the name as\ngiven and fall back to its lowercase form. Non-string and non-string-array\nvalues count as absent.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#customHeaderCredentials\">customHeaderCredentials()</a> ⇒ <code>Credentials</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Credentials from the custom headers: returned only when both <code>username</code> and\n<code>password</code> are non-empty strings (absent/non-string/empty means &quot;not provided&quot;).</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#bodyCredentials\">bodyCredentials()</a> ⇒ <code>Credentials</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Credentials from a parsed request body: <code>body.auth.username</code> / <code>body.auth.password</code>,\nread with own-property checks only (a crafted body with inherited <code>auth</code> is not trusted).</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#timingSafeCompare\">timingSafeCompare()</a> ⇒ <code>boolean</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Compare two strings in constant time. Both buffers are padded to the same\nlength so <code>timingSafeEqual</code> runs unconditionally — it neither throws nor\nshort-circuits, so timing reveals neither the lengths nor the value.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"BasicAuthGuard\"></a>\n\n## BasicAuthGuard\nGuards a route with the HTTP Basic authentication scheme (RFC 7617), wrapping\nthe [`basic-auth`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/basic-auth) package (`parse`).\n\nCredentials are resolved in order (first source that yields credentials wins):\n\n1. the standard `Authorization` header via `parse()` — when the header is\n   present it is authoritative (an empty value falls through, a malformed one\n   rejects the request);\n2. the custom `headerNames` headers (`x-auth-username`/`x-auth-password` by\n   default) when both values are non-empty strings;\n3. the request body `auth.username`/`auth.password` when `body: true` is set.\n\nOn success: sets `req.user` to the validated credentials.\nOn failure: sets `WWW-Authenticate` on the response and throws `UnauthorizedException`.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: src/basic-auth.guard.ts:139  \ndist: dist/basic-auth.guard.js:89\n\n* [BasicAuthGuard](#BasicAuthGuard)\n    * [.expectedPairs](#BasicAuthGuard+expectedPairs) ⇒ <code>{ name: Buffer; pass: Buffer; }[]</code>\n    * [.canActivate(context)](#BasicAuthGuard+canActivate) ⇒ <code>boolean</code>\n    * [.resolveCredentials()](#BasicAuthGuard+resolveCredentials) ⇒ <code>Credentials</code>\n    * [.fallbackSources()](#BasicAuthGuard+fallbackSources) ⇒ <code>CredentialSource[]</code>\n    * [.reject()](#BasicAuthGuard+reject) ⇒ <code>never</code>\n    * [.challenge()](#BasicAuthGuard+challenge) ⇒ <code>string</code>\n    * [.isValidCredentials()](#BasicAuthGuard+isValidCredentials) ⇒ <code>boolean</code>\n\n<a name=\"BasicAuthGuard+expectedPairs\"></a>\n\n### basicAuthGuard.expectedPairs ⇒ <code>{ name: Buffer; pass: Buffer; }[]</code>\nExpected credentials as buffers, cached on first use (options/environment are fixed after construction).\n\n**Kind**: instance property of [<code>BasicAuthGuard</code>](#BasicAuthGuard)  \nsrc: src/basic-auth.guard.ts:224  \ndist: dist/basic-auth.guard.js:169\n<a name=\"BasicAuthGuard+canActivate\"></a>\n\n### basicAuthGuard.canActivate(context) ⇒ <code>boolean</code>\nNestJS guard entry point: resolves and validates credentials from the request.\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>BasicAuthGuard</code>](#BasicAuthGuard)  \n**Returns**: <code>boolean</code> - `true` when authenticated; throws `UnauthorizedException` (401) with a\n  `WWW-Authenticate` challenge otherwise.  \n\n| Param | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| context | <code>ExecutionContext</code> | The NestJS execution context (HTTP request/response). |\n\nsrc: src/basic-auth.guard.ts:157  \ndist: dist/basic-auth.guard.js:108\n<a name=\"BasicAuthGuard+resolveCredentials\"></a>\n\n### basicAuthGuard.resolveCredentials() ⇒ <code>Credentials</code>\nResolve credentials in order:\n\n1. the standard `Authorization` header — when present it is authoritative\n   (a present-but-unparseable value rejects the request, no fallback);\n2. the custom `headerNames` headers, when both values are non-empty strings;\n3. the request body pair, when `body: true` is set.\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>BasicAuthGuard</code>](#BasicAuthGuard)  \nsrc: src/basic-auth.guard.ts:176  \ndist: dist/basic-auth.guard.js:126\n<a name=\"BasicAuthGuard+fallbackSources\"></a>\n\n### basicAuthGuard.fallbackSources() ⇒ <code>CredentialSource[]</code>\nFallback credential sources, consulted in order after the standard header.\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>BasicAuthGuard</code>](#BasicAuthGuard)  \nsrc: src/basic-auth.guard.ts:188  \ndist: dist/basic-auth.guard.js:138\n<a name=\"BasicAuthGuard+reject\"></a>\n\n### basicAuthGuard.reject() ⇒ <code>never</code>\nSets the `WWW-Authenticate: Basic realm=\"...\"` challenge (realm escaped per RFC 7617) and throws a 401.\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>BasicAuthGuard</code>](#BasicAuthGuard)  \nsrc: src/basic-auth.guard.ts:196  \ndist: dist/basic-auth.guard.js:145\n<a name=\"BasicAuthGuard+challenge\"></a>\n\n### basicAuthGuard.challenge() ⇒ <code>string</code>\nThe `WWW-Authenticate` challenge string with the realm escaped per RFC 7617.\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>BasicAuthGuard</code>](#BasicAuthGuard)  \nsrc: src/basic-auth.guard.ts:207  \ndist: dist/basic-auth.guard.js:156\n<a name=\"BasicAuthGuard+isValidCredentials\"></a>\n\n### basicAuthGuard.isValidCredentials() ⇒ <code>boolean</code>\nConstant-time check of the provided credentials against every expected pair.\nBoth comparisons always run and are length-padded, so a mismatch in username\ndoes not skip the password check (no timing oracle on the username or on the\nexpected password length).\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>BasicAuthGuard</code>](#BasicAuthGuard)  \nsrc: src/basic-auth.guard.ts:246  \ndist: dist/basic-auth.guard.js:188\n<a name=\"readHeader\"></a>\n\n## readHeader() ⇒ <code>string</code>\nRead a header by name: Node normalizes names to lowercase, so try the name as\ngiven and fall back to its lowercase form. Non-string and non-string-array\nvalues count as absent.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \nsrc: src/basic-auth.guard.ts:78  \ndist: dist/basic-auth.guard.js:30\n<a name=\"customHeaderCredentials\"></a>\n\n## customHeaderCredentials() ⇒ <code>Credentials</code>\nCredentials from the custom headers: returned only when both `username` and\n`password` are non-empty strings (absent/non-string/empty means \"not provided\").\n\n**Kind**: global function  \nsrc: src/basic-auth.guard.ts:89  \ndist: dist/basic-auth.guard.js:41\n<a name=\"bodyCredentials\"></a>\n\n## bodyCredentials() ⇒ <code>Credentials</code>\nCredentials from a parsed request body: `body.auth.username` / `body.auth.password`,\nread with own-property checks only (a crafted body with inherited `auth` is not trusted).\n\n**Kind**: global function  \nsrc: src/basic-auth.guard.ts:99  \ndist: dist/basic-auth.guard.js:50\n<a name=\"timingSafeCompare\"></a>\n\n## timingSafeCompare() ⇒ <code>boolean</code>\nCompare two strings in constant time. Both buffers are padded to the same\nlength so `timingSafeEqual` runs unconditionally — it neither throws nor\nshort-circuits, so timing reveals neither the lengths nor the value.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \nsrc: src/basic-auth.guard.ts:115  \ndist: dist/basic-auth.guard.js:67\n","symbols":14,"lastUsed":1795601953481}},"version":1}